# DENY-BY-DEFAULT, not a growing blocklist. The previous version of this
# file excluded specific known-large paths individually and missed
# .hf_cache/ — a 9.3GB local HuggingFace model cache dir this session
# created but that nothing had ever inventoried — which then transferred
# into the build context wholesale and (combined with an already RAM-
# constrained machine) caused a near-crisis: RAM to 0.34GB free / 97% used
# mid-build. A blocklist only ever excludes what you already knew to name.
# An allowlist is safe by construction against the NEXT unknown large
# directory, not just the ones caught so far.
*

# --- Explicitly re-included: exactly what Dockerfile.api/.ui need ---
# requirements.txt (full) for Dockerfile.ui; requirements-api.txt (scoped)
# for Dockerfile.api — see that file's header for why they're different.
!requirements.txt
!requirements-api.txt
!api/
!core/
!ui/
!models/
!policies/
!policies.json
!policy_rules.json

# Re-including a directory does not recurse into ITS subdirectories'
# ignored contents by Docker's rules, so caches nested inside re-included
# dirs still need their own exclusion.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/

# Secrets — belt and suspenders even under allowlist, since none of the
# re-included paths above should ever contain these, but a stray misplaced
# file must not ship regardless.
**/api_keys.json
**/tenants.json
**/.env
